.TH START-MU2EDAQ-BIGREDBOX.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 2.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh, start_daq_alert.sh \- start the Big Red Box alert listener in the background
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh
.br
.B start_daq_alert.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
Control\-room start script, run as
.BR "crs\-app start bigredbox" .
.B start_daq_alert.sh
is a git symbolic link to this script, kept for the old name; both behave
identically.
.PP
The script, in order:
.IP 1. 4
changes to its own directory, so that the relative default
.I config/tts_templates.yaml
is found;
.IP 2. 4
exports
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
(default 37020) and
.B DISPLAY
(default
.BR :0 )
if they are not already set;
.IP 3. 4
exits 0 with "already running" if
.I /tmp/daq_alert.pid
names a live process, otherwise removes the PID file;
.IP 4. 4
probes the UDP port by binding it from Python and exits 1 if the bind fails,
printing the
.BR lsof (8)
holder when available;
.IP 5. 4
launches, in order of preference,
.IR venv/bin/mu2edaq\-bigredbox ,
.B mu2edaq\-bigredbox
on
.BR PATH ,
or
.B python3 daq_alert.py
from the checkout, under
.BR nohup (1)
with standard output and error appended to
.IR /tmp/daq_alert.log ;
.IP 6. 4
waits one second and exits 1, printing the last three log lines, if the
process has already died.
.PP
.B Limitations.
The port probe sets
.BR SO_REUSEADDR ,
so on Linux it succeeds even while another listener holds the port, and a
second listener is started.
The PID and log paths are fixed: the script does not honour
.B DAQ_ALERT_PID_FILE
or
.BR DAQ_ALERT_LOG_FILE ,
although the listener itself does.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/daq_alert.pid
Checked for a running listener; written by the listener, not by this script.
.TP
.I /tmp/daq_alert.log
The listener's standard output and error are appended here.
.TP
.I venv/
Virtual environment created by
.BR bootstrap.sh (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
UDP port the listener binds; default 37020.
Exported by
.B crs\-app
from
.IR apps.yaml .
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 display for the alert windows; default
.BR :0 .
On a host whose console session is not
.BR :0 ,
set it explicitly.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listener was started and is still alive after one second, or a listener
named in the PID file is already running.
.TP
.B 1
The port probe failed, or the listener died within one second (for example
Qt could not open the display, or
.I libpulse.so.0
is missing).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh
CRS_PORT_UDP=37030 DISPLAY=:1 ./start\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh
tail \-n 20 /tmp/daq_alert.log
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox (1),
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-bigredbox.sh (1),
.BR bootstrap.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
